course: dictionary
lesson: 14769
title: Protector: the one who keeps you safe
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A protector is a person or animal that keeps someone or something safe from harm. The word comes from protect, which means to guard. Look for the clues in the sentence: what is being kept safe, and from what?
explain: «The mother bird spread her wings over her chicks to keep them dry.» The mother bird is a protector. She guards her chicks from the rain and from danger. The protector is the one doing the guarding.
explain: A protector can also be a thing. «Dan wore shin protectors to stop his legs getting hurt in the football match.» Here the shin protectors are things that stop injuries. You may see the word in a phone shop too: a screen protector guards your phone's screen from scratches.
explain: In history, the word has a special meaning. Oliver Cromwell was called Lord Protector, and he ruled England, Scotland and Ireland in the 1650s. When you see a capital letter and a title, check the history clue before you decide what the word means.
fact: Protector means a person or animal that keeps someone or something safe from harm.
fact: A protector can also be a thing, such as a screen protector, a gum shield or shin protectors.
fact: «Badger was the protector of the younger animals in the wood.» In the story, Badger guards the weak.
fact: In history, Lord Protector was the title of Oliver Cromwell, who ruled England, Scotland and Ireland in the 1650s.
fact: Clue words such as guard, safe and harm often show you that the word is about keeping something from danger.
exercise: «The mother bird spread her wings to keep her chicks dry.» What is the mother bird acting as? | A thief | A visitor passing by | A teacher who gives lessons | *A protector who keeps her chicks safe
exercise: «Dan wore a gum shield to protect his teeth in rugby.» What is a gum shield in this sentence? | A kind of sports team | Something that makes you run faster | A score in the game | *A protector that stops your teeth getting hurt
exercise: «Badger was the protector of the younger animals in the wood.» Find and copy the word that names the one who guards the young animals. | animals | *Badger | younger | wood
test: In 1653, Oliver Cromwell was given a special title. Which title did he hold? | King of England | *Lord Protector | Lord Mayor | Prince of Wales
test: Which of these is a protector? | A cup of hot chocolate | *A shin pad that guards your legs from kicks | A book about dragons | A sunny day at the beach
exam: Mia says a protector can only be a person. Is she right? | Yes, only people can be protectors | Yes, but only grown-ups | No, it is only a word from history books | *No, a protector can be a person, an animal or a thing like a screen protector
